WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
幕布就要打开。胸口一阵砰砰跳。
The curtain is about to open. Your heart is pounding.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
这是害怕，还是兴奋？
Is this fear, or excitement?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.700
上台做报告时，心跳加快可以伴随紧张。
A racing heart can accompany anxiety before a presentation.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.000
期待演出时，同样的信号也可以伴随兴奋。
The same signal can accompany excitement before a performance.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
当要求很高、可用时间和支持很少，压力可能升高。
Stress may rise when demands are high and time or support is limited.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
现场条件和身体状态，都值得一起看。
Look at both the situation and what your body is doing.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.600
把“心跳快就说明我要失败”换成“我正在为上台做准备”。
Try reading the racing heart as preparation to go on stage.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.000
认知重评改变的是你对这次信号的解释。
Cognitive reappraisal changes your interpretation of the signal.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.100
有些压力需要改现场。可以请求多一次排练，或者减少任务。
Some stress calls for changing the situation. Ask for rehearsal or a smaller task.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.000
换个解释和调整条件，可以同时做。
You can reframe the situation and change its conditions.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
下次心跳快时，先说说现在发生了什么，再决定下一步。
When your heart races, name the situation before choosing your next step.
